      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Testing for subtle, embedded frequencies within complex building infrastructure without alerting personnel is very difficult and potentially unsafe. Professional equipment, such as sensitive spectrum analyzers, is required to detect very low or specific modulation patterns in operational noise. If you suspect technical malpractice, collecting detailed, time-stamped recordings is useful evidence, but direct physical probing of HVAC or electrical systems carries significant danger. You might consider formally logging your observations through official tenant complaint channels while keeping your recordings as documentation.",
